<title>UK: UK undecided on Post Office privatisation - Major.</title>
<headline>UK undecided on Post Office privatisation - Major.</headline>
<dateline>BOURNEMOUTH, England 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister John Major said on Wednesday his government had not decided yet whether to modernise the Post Office via full-scale privatisation or by introducing private capital in various ways.</p>
<p>In a question and answer session at the Conservative party's annual conference, Major also said proposals outlined by Trade Secretary Ian Lang for a possible ban on strikes in public- sector monopolies did not constitute &quot;union-bashing&quot;.</p>
<p>But he said the government was looking at ways of ensuring the consumer was protected from what he called &quot;unreasonable&quot; strikes.</p>
<p>-- Bournemouth Newsroom +44 1202 319 935</p>
